WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.240
Hey everyone, welcome to Tesla Short's Time, Daily Episode 520 for June 23, 2026.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.340
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver. Here's what you need to know about Tesla today.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:18.440
Finland's transport agency is now testing whether Tesla FSD can manage icy roads and obscured markings

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:24.360
before any rollout to local owners. The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration has

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:31.040
opened a probe into a fatal crash in Texas. Investigators are looking at whether full self-driving

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:37.320
was active and how the system behaved in the moments leading up to the incident. Tesla has stated

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:43.800
that the driver overrode the system during the event. The investigation also reaches into questions

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:51.360
around the Robotaxi program and plans for unsupervised FSD operation. Shares reacted to the news

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:57.940
as broader regulatory attention on the technology continues. While US regulators examine one crash,

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:04.680
European regulators are watching real-world sales momentum. Tesla posted a sharp rebound in European

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:11.460
sales during May. Registrations more than doubled compared with the previous month. The Model Y

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:17.480
moved back into the top three models sold across the region. Those gains arrived against a mixed

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:24.480
overall electric vehicle market. BYD continues to expand its presence with new models and pricing

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:30.260
in the same markets. The numbers mark a clear reversal from softer results seen in April across

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:36.380
several countries. Sales strength in Europe contrasts with the stricter local testing now underway in

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:44.260
Finland. Finland's Trafacom has begun evaluating Tesla FSD under winter conditions. The agency will

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:50.300
test performance on ice, snow, and roads with obscured markings before any owner roll out.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:56.380
The review builds on the Dutch Provisional approval from April but adds stricter local safety checks.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:03.960
If cleared, the software would reach roughly 6,500 newer Tesla models already registered in Finland.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:13.360
Drivers must remain fully attentive no matter the outcome of the evaluation. This connects to the

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:20.220
approval we have followed in recent episodes. Regulators evaluating driver assistance systems must

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:26.860
decide how much local road data is required before granting approval. Finland's approach starts from

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:33.180
an existing Dutch Provisional clearance yet adds explicit tests for snow, ice, and obscured

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:39.660
markings that the baseline review did not cover. That extra layer reveals a basic tension between

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:45.560
broad training data and the need for region-specific validation when pavement conditions and

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:52.340
signage quality change sharply. The practical result is a staggered rollout even inside the EU.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:58.840
Only newer vehicles already on finished roads would receive the software if Trafacom signs off

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:05.220
and drivers remain fully responsible at every moment. This structure limits immediate scale while

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:10.860
creating a measurable safety data set under winter conditions that other markets can later reference.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:16.020
For Tesla, the cost shows up in deployment timing rather than hardware changes.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:22.340
Each additional national review extends the period before unsupervised operation can generate

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:31.020
revenue at volume. An analyst forecast puts Tesla on track for 392,900 vehicle deliveries in the

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:36.200
second quarter. The estimate comes while production continues at the three main factories.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:42.520
No model by model breakdown was included in the projection. The figure will be compared directly

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:49.740
against Tesla's official delivery report once released. Rivian plans to launch the R3 compact adventure

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:56.580
SUV as a direct competitor to Tesla models. The vehicle combines off-road capability with a lower

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:03.160
price point than current Rivian offerings. Rivian positions the R3 to capture buyers seeking style

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:08.940
and utility in a smaller package. Production timing and final pricing remain to be confirmed.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:15.620
The R3 announcement arrives as Tesla continues volume production of the model Y and Model 3

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:22.080
at its main factories. Reports note the R3 targets a segment that overlaps with existing Tesla

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:27.780
crossover demand. No specific launch date for the R3 has been set in the current coverage.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:34.760
Reports outline a stretched Model Y variant expected for 2027 with added rear legroom.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:40.980
The longer wheelbase version would target markets that favor three-row or larger family vehicles.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:47.440
No official confirmation or pricing details have been released by Tesla. Production would likely

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:54.660
occur at existing overseas factories. The Model YL concept follows ongoing demand for more

00:04:54.660 --> 00:05:00.820
spacious variants in certain regions, earlier Model Y updates focused on range and performance

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:07.860
rather than wheelbase changes. Any 2027 introduction would depend on factory tooling decisions

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:15.180
not yet detailed. Vehicle volumes remain central, yet Tesla is also locking in large energy stored

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:22.540
orders. Net power signed a $5 billion agreement for 25 gigawatt hours of Megapack storage.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:29.040
The deal covers large scale projects across multiple regions. Deliveries and installations will

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:34.860
stretch over several years. The order adds to Tesla's growing energy storage backlog outside

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:40.940
a vehicle production. Domestic manufacturing strength sits alongside new app features aimed at

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:48.640
the Model 3 and Model Y once again top the American-made index compiled by cars.com.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:53.780
This marks the sixth consecutive year the two models have taken the top two spots.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:58.400
Tesla vehicles have led the ranking every year since the list began.

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:04.900
Tariffs and the end of the federal EV tax credit reduced representation from the Detroit 3 on

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:10.760
this year's index. While owners engage with new features, real world data on battery behavior

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:17.800
continues to emerge and X rental Model Y lost roughly 20% of battery capacity in its first two

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:23.540
years of heavy use. Subsequent data shows the degradation rate has nearly plateaued.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:29.440
The pattern suggests high utilization vehicles may stabilize after initial capacity loss.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:35.380
Owners tracking similar packs will watch whether the plateau holds over additional mileage.

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:41.700
The example comes from a vehicle subjected to rental fleet conditions before private ownership.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:48.140
No broader fleet-wide statistics were included in the report. The findings focus on one vehicle's

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:55.940
capacity trend over time. A Cybertruck completed a 350-mile boat-towing trip while averaging 700 watt

00:06:55.940 --> 00:07:04.200
hours per mile. Maintaining 55 miles per hour proved more efficient overall and higher speeds despite

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:09.680
the added load. The test highlights real-world towing consumption under highway conditions.

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:17.680
No official Tesla towing range claims were referenced in the report. The load totaled 6,500 pounds

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:23.200
for the full distance. Efficiency measurements were recorded throughout the run at consistent speeds.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:28.380
The results add to owner-collected data on Cybertruck performance with trailers.

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:35.180
A Delaware bill would authorize DNREC to provide financial assistance for Tesla purchases by

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:41.760
lower income residents. The measure aims to expand EV access beyond current federal incentives.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:47.580
Note funding amount or program details have been finalized. Passage would create a state-level

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:53.940
channel for Tesla adoption support. The proposal targets households that may not qualify for existing

00:07:53.940 --> 00:08:00.440
rebates. Sponsors frame the bill as a way to broaden electric vehicle availability at the state level.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:07.340
No timeline for a vote has been announced in the current reports. Tesla added charge stats to

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:13.360
the mobile app. The update lets owners view road trips on a map and track charging milestones.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:17.500
New badges are earned by visiting specific superchargers.

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:23.580
Owners reach the view through the Tesla app under charging and then charge stats and badges.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:29.660
The feature builds on the existing charging passport by adding visual trip data and milestone

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:37.920
rewards. Tesla also launched a 2026 free supercharging contest. The competition awards free supercharging

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:43.940
miles based on charging activity. Owners have already noted adjusting longer routes to collect new

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:49.960
supercharger visits. The program layers additional gamification onto the passport collection mechanic.

